  "about": "Hardware Sniffer reports and ACPI tables the builder is tested with (tests/run-fixtures.sh). Public reports and tables are fetched at a pinned commit and checked by SHA-256 (tests/fetch_fixtures.py); they are not copied into this repository. z790-b580/Report.json is ours: the test machine (efi/sample-z790) written in Hardware Sniffer's format, with no serial numbers, UUIDs or MAC addresses. A fixture's 'replace' swaps whole top-level sections of the report, to put an Arc card where the public PC had another GPU. No public ACPI dump of a Z790 board was found; the Z790 fixtures use the ASUS B660 dump (same maker, the 600/700-series PCH, the slot named \\_SB.PC00.PEG1 as on the test machine). card_port is the ACPI path of the card's upstream port given to efi.sh as a fact for the stage-4 test (on a real PC efi.sh reads it from ioreg): the slot's root port and PEGP below it, as each board's DSDT names them.",
